==Battleground==
*5 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Wild Doge]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*5 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Wild Doge]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Helmut Krabbe]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You are strongly recommended to collect all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] before attempting this stage.

Start by stalling for money before hitting the enemy base. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] is a perfect choice for a meatshield; it is [[Strong Against]] the majority of the enemies and, when upgraded to True Form, even [[Immune to Slow|Immune to]] the boss's [[Slow]] effect. Crustaceous Scissorex can cover a wide range with its attack, so using peons as stepping stones is a good choice to attack it with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]]. Despite not being [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], both the Wild Doges and Scissorex can also take significant damage from [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]].

A great strategy would be stacking 3-4 [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cats]] before summoning the boss and let them attack, effectively perma-[[Freeze|Freezing]] it, securing an easy victory. Level 30 Seafarer can tank at least 3 hits from Scissorex, giving you plenty of room to clear the peons and let them permanently Freeze the boss.

